{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 13, "text": "I have corrected the four drawing-related issues identified in the previous review.\n\nFor FIG. 2, I revised the figure brief to correctly depict the support mechanism for the thermal module, ensuring it is supported by the shell side walls and not the product tray, consistent with the detailed description. I also removed descriptions of elements that were not being rendered and corrected the description of the product tray to ensure it is rendered as a fully hatched pan. I also added the `shell floor 12` to this figure for consistency.\n\nFor FIG. 5, I clarified the instruction in the figure brief to ensure the tray side wall extends to the bottom of the drawing area as intended.\n\nFor FIG. 6, I resolved the issue of converging leader lines by providing separate and distinct endpoint targets for the numerals for the product tray (20) and the tray side wall (24). I also provided a more specific target for the leader line for the condensate channel (70) to resolve its reported misplacement.\n\nFor FIG. 7, to prevent the rendering of spurious text artifacts, I strengthened the negative constraint against drawing any text and refined the description of the spring element to make its coiled geometry unambiguous and distinct from any letter-like shapes.\n\nThese changes have been made directly to the corresponding files in the `figures/` directory. The detailed description and numeral list were already consistent with these corrections."}
{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 14, "text": "I have corrected the four drawing-related issues identified in the previous review.\n\nFor FIG. 2, I revised the figure brief to correctly depict the support mechanism for the thermal module, ensuring it is supported by the shell side walls and not the product tray, consistent with the detailed description. I also removed descriptions of elements that were not being rendered and corrected the description of the product tray to ensure it is rendered as a fully hatched pan. I also added the `shell floor 12` to this figure for consistency.\n\nFor FIG. 5, I clarified the instruction in the figure brief to ensure the tray side wall extends to the bottom of the drawing area as intended.\n\nFor FIG. 6, I resolved the issue of converging leader lines by providing separate and distinct endpoint targets for the numerals for the product tray (20) and the tray side wall (24). I also provided a more specific target for the leader line for the condensate channel (70) to resolve its reported misplacement.\n\nFor FIG. 7, to prevent the rendering of spurious text artifacts, I strengthened the negative constraint against drawing any text and refined the description of the spring element to make its coiled geometry unambiguous and distinct from any letter-like shapes.\n\nThese changes have been made directly to the corresponding files in the `figures/` directory. The detailed description and numeral list were already consistent with these corrections. The draft should now pass the automated checks."}
